  "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations. \n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I represents a translation by $3$ units to the left and $1$ unit upward. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II represents a dilation of scale factor $2$ and center $O.$ Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III represents a rotation by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise around the point $O.$ Thus, it is a rigid motion and, therefore, a similarity transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
